      "title": "Passing Data With Props & Dynamic Content",
      "lectureOrder": 60,
      "videoOrder": 56,
      "sourceHash": "ab3e1c7783ae552abe018703d105f87532f465c9040cd6367f100ff100548b88",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 4.61,
          "en": "To make our component a bit more configurable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.61,
          "end": 7.04,
          "en": "and accept different data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.04,
          "end": 9.72,
          "en": "we in the end wanna utilize a concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.72,
          "end": 11.62,
          "en": "which we know from the function world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.62,
          "end": 14.74,
          "en": "and from standard HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.74,
          "end": 18.37,
          "en": "In the place where we use Todo, so in this app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.37,
          "end": 21.05,
          "en": "it would be nice if we could add an attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.05,
          "end": 24.91,
          "en": "like text or title, totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.91,
          "end": 28.48,
          "en": "Let's go with text and then set this to some value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.48,
          "end": 31.293,
          "en": "like Learn React on the first Todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.36,
          "end": 36.1,
          "en": "then Master React on the second Todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.1,
          "end": 38.07,
          "en": "and let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.07,
          "end": 42.543,
          "en": "Explore the full React course, in the third Todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.543,
          "end": 45.26,
          "en": "Now, it would be nice if you could do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.26,
          "end": 48.91,
          "en": "But if I add this here, in App.js and save it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.91,
          "end": 52.45,
          "en": "this has no effect on what we see on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.45,
          "end": 53.45,
          "en": "The reason for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.45,
          "end": 57.53,
          "en": "is that we're setting these custom attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.53,
          "end": 59.39,
          "en": "but then the Todo.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.39,
          "end": 63.61,
          "en": "we have no code that would pick up those values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.61,
          "end": 68.05,
          "en": "Nonetheless, this is how you do pass data into a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.05,
          "end": 71.17,
          "en": "We just also need to write some code in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.17,
          "end": 75.46000000000001,
          "en": "to then accept and use those received values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.46000000000001,
          "end": 79.87,
          "en": "And we do that with a concept called props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.87,
          "end": 83.69,
          "en": "We accept the parameter in our function component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.69,
          "end": 86.15,
          "en": "and in every function component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.15,
          "end": 88.49,
          "en": "we can accept that parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.49,
          "end": 91.56,
          "en": "and that parameter is typically called props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.56,
          "end": 93.18,
          "en": "You can name it whatever you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.18,
          "end": 95.55,
          "en": "since it's your code, but it's called props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.55,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "because this React concept is called props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 100.7,
          "en": "This will be an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.7,
          "end": 102.97999999999999,
          "en": "Props will be a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.97999999999999,
          "end": 106.84,
          "en": "where all the attributes added on the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.84,
          "end": 109.86,
          "en": "are in the end available as key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.86,
          "end": 112.00999999999999,
          "en": "in this props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "So here, these attribute names will be the keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 119.27000000000001,
          "en": "and the values will be the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.27000000000001,
          "end": 122.16,
          "en": "So props inside of the Todo component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.16,
          "end": 125.6,
          "en": "will be an object now, that has a text property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.6,
          "end": 129.64,
          "en": "and then different values for this text property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.64,
          "end": 132.21,
          "en": "And if you named this attribute differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 133.23,
          "en": "that's also okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.23,
          "end": 136.31,
          "en": "you will then have a property of that name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.31,
          "end": 138.64,
          "en": "in your props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.64,
          "end": 141.32,
          "en": "So therefore now here, in this h2 tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.32,
          "end": 142.69,
          "en": "we wanna output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.69,
          "end": 146.75,
          "en": "this text we're getting on this props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.75,
          "end": 148.34,
          "en": "Now in standard JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.34,
          "end": 152.69,
          "en": "we access object properties with the dot notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.69,
          "end": 155.42000000000002,
          "en": "So we could output props.text here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.42000000000002,
          "end": 158.63,
          "en": "to access the text property in the props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.63,
          "end": 162.49,
          "en": "and therefore the values stored in this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.49,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "But if we do this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 167.3,
          "en": "we just see props.text as our output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.3,
          "end": 169.84,
          "en": "The reason for this is that everything here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.84,
          "end": 174.84,
          "en": "in this JSX block is treated as HTML elements or plain text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.63,
          "end": 178.32,
          "en": "The good news, however is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.32,
          "end": 182.42,
          "en": "that we can also output dynamic expressions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.42,
          "end": 184.38,
          "en": "as part of the JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.38,
          "end": 186.47,
          "en": "We can tell React that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.47,
          "end": 189.81,
          "en": "something should not be treated as plain text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.81,
          "end": 192.34,
          "en": "but instead as a JavaScript expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.34,
          "end": 194.35,
          "en": "that should be evaluated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.35,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "And we do this with a special syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 200.78,
          "en": "inside of this JSX code, which looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.78,
          "end": 205.78,
          "en": "Opening and closing curly braces, single curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.06,
          "end": 208.52,
          "en": "And between those braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.52,
          "end": 211.47,
          "en": "you can have any JavaScript expression you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.47,
          "end": 214.45,
          "en": "like for example, two plus two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.45,
          "end": 217.21,
          "en": "Now this will not be treated as plain text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.21,
          "end": 220.57,
          "en": "but instead it will be executed as JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.57,
          "end": 224.403,
          "en": "So if I save, we see four, the result of this expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.76,
          "end": 229.76,
          "en": "Now you can have any single line expression in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.76,
          "end": 232.27,
          "en": "but you can't have any block statements here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.27,
          "end": 235.81,
          "en": "So adding a if check here would not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.81,
          "end": 240.21,
          "en": "But what does work is referring to props.text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.21,
          "end": 242.31,
          "en": "So simply outputting the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.31,
          "end": 246.263,
          "en": "of accessing this text property on the props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.43,
          "end": 250.23,
          "en": "If we add this code and save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.23,
          "end": 254.193,
          "en": "we see our different texts here for the different Todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.23,
          "end": 258.09,
          "en": "And now we built our own truly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.09,
          "end": 262.6,
          "en": "reusable React component here, the Todo component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.6,
          "end": 265.12,
          "en": "It is truly reusable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.12,
          "end": 268.72,
          "en": "because now it does not just have some hard coded structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.72,
          "end": 270.847,
          "en": "and text inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.847,
          "end": 275.43,
          "en": "but also some dynamic code using this core concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.43,
          "end": 278.3,
          "en": "built into React, the props concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.3,
          "end": 281.15999999999997,
          "en": "for accepting data from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.15999999999997,
          "end": 284.193,
          "en": "So from the place where it is being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.04,
          "end": 287.88,
          "en": "That is a key concept, this props concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.88,
          "end": 291.92,
          "en": "and that is how you build re-usable custom elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.92,
          "end": 294.32,
          "en": "re-usable components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.32,
          "end": 298.42,
          "en": "And that's there for a major first step here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.42,
          "end": 301.37,
          "en": "Now let's make sure that we handle events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.37,
          "end": 303.7,
          "en": "that we handle our click on the delete button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.7,
          "end": 307.12,
          "en": "and that we then also change something on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.12,
          "end": 308.96,
          "en": "when the button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 308.96,
          "end": 313.43,
          "en": "To be precise that we present this nice overlay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.43,
          "end": 315.423,
          "en": "when that delete button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
